Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Gravitational corrections to matter propagators", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b1870694-48db-4d3b-a510-3651c3d5bcda"],

Cell["\<\
Explore the graviton contributions to scalar, fermion, massive-vector, \
massless-vector, gluon and quark two-point functions. Follow one sector at a \
time to learn vertex assembly, loop reduction and result inspection.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a8a7cfe-8200-4a31-b209-fb4fb5d419c3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"faffbe22-3228-4446-8054-da7dcb431001"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1273878a-8bc7-432d-9193-63868c6c4479"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{4.000099972767213*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"8168dc49-3c37-47ba-90a2-b4cd58a1a16a"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook requires FORM on the kernel\[CloseCurlyQuote]s PATH. \
CalcFormCalculate performs bosonic algebra and Lorentz contractions; TFORM is \
used automatically when available. FeynCalc handles loop reduction and any \
Dirac or colour algebra before the bosonic coefficients are sent to FORM.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.00009997597785*^9},ExpressionUUID->"9ce37baa-d571-4f6d-9856-074d3da8aa14"],

Cell["\<\
Explicit expands FeynCalc propagator shorthand before export. SUNSimplify \
contracts colour indices, and DiracSimplify with DiracOrder -> True reduces \
and orders open Dirac chains. Collect sends only the bosonic coefficients of \
the remaining DiracGamma or SUNDelta structures to CalcFormCalculate. Loop \
reduction stays in FeynCalc. SUNNToCACF -> False keeps colour factors in terms \
of SUNN, matching the displayed reference formulas.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7b453c41-dc11-4817-91ff-503866d6a4f9"],

Cell["\<\
The external momentum is p, the loop momentum is k, and m denotes the matter \
mass where present. Repeated Lorentz or colour indices are summed. TID[..., k, \
ToPaVe -> True] reduces tensor integrals to scalar A0 and B0 functions. In \
FeynCalc\[CloseCurlyQuote]s convention these expressions retain the i \[Pi]\
\.b2 normalisation; no (2\[Pi])^(-D) loop-measure prefactor is inserted here. \
Keep D symbolic during reduction. Setting D -> 4 in a displayed coefficient \
is not a Laurent expansion, UV subtraction, or a renormalised answer.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0507f9a5-9183-4ead-baed-4ec8c2e29dfa"],

Cell["\<\
FeynGrav supplies the vertex and propagator normalisations, including i and \
\[Kappa]. The default gravitational gauge parameter is GaugeFixingEpsilon = \
2. The displayed diagram weights are retained from the original example; the \
notebook does not derive their combinatorics.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fe8fc526-322d-44ff-9051-b91f1746cf40"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"importSUNYM", "[", "2", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1d09ce57-263f-4350-acc3-ff437df9d50d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Scalar", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8e77db67-e2e7-4c7b-961c-bb57ad3b0946"],

Cell["\<\
The external matter legs are amputated. The internal graviton and matter \
propagators are shown explicitly in each bubble integrand.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d89b8a2f-3809-4789-b62d-ab15220c483c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tadpole", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"201aaf28-ffa8-4f8c-bd19-79fd346a3c50"],

Cell["\<\
Close the two graviton legs of the contact vertex with one graviton \
propagator. The massless gravitational tadpole is scaleless in dimensional \
regularisation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bb3bfda8-2055-4226-a429-0237949bf1e9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ScalarPolarizationOperator1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]"}], 
         "}"}], ",", "p", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "k"}], 
       "]"}]}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d862d513-aebc-4cdb-894b-9701d7ea6ddb"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bubble", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"675477cf-f6c3-45b9-b65e-0d3d2d4177d5"],

Cell["\<\
Join two three-point vertices with a graviton and a matter propagator. Dirac \
products use Dot; do not replace them by ordinary multiplication. \
GravitonFermionVertex takes graviton triples {index, index, incoming \
momentum}; include these momenta even when older examples list only the \
indices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5039a59a-f6e0-41b7-bf44-876a6ab287e3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ScalarPolarizationOperator2", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "}"}], ",", "p", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "k"}], 
       "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"ScalarPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d65f7751-1f90-4c53-a16d-50ab0bcf538a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Combined operator", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"cdcecd5c-d342-4c6c-942a-93389dffc137"],

Cell["\<\
Add the stored tadpole and bubble terms and collect their scalar master \
integrals.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4397736f-9e51-46be-999b-14703c19782b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ScalarPolarizationOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ScalarPolarizationOperator1", "[", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", "m"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"ScalarPolarizationOperator2", "[", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"C0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#1", ",", "m", ",", "Factor"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b098053b-6424-446e-8eb5-670eaf771c36"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Display or compare the result", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"98e1c7b1-c55b-4e71-94bc-3e7dc67ad5a7"],

Cell["\<\
The four-dimensional coefficient expression retains unevaluated scalar loop \
integrals. A True comparison confirms the written reference in this gauge; it \
does not perform UV renormalisation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"72d01624-d273-46b2-9671-bcdcc6e03021"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ScalarPolarizationOperator", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "m"}], "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"GaugeFixingEpsilon", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], ")"}], "\[Equal]", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
        RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], "-", 
       FractionBox[
        SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], "2"]}], ")"}], " ", "\[ImaginaryI]", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", "2"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"B0", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
        RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], ",", "0", ",", 
       SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}], "]"}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", "2"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], " ", "\[ImaginaryI]", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", "2"], " ", 
     RowBox[{"A0", "[", 
      SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000099995085911*^9, 4.0001000041775007`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b265f251-917d-4cf8-949e-4aa2c82eb597"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Dirac fermion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3876be3c-37e7-41c5-94e7-05091a0a2674"],

Cell["\<\
The external matter legs are amputated. The internal graviton and matter \
propagators are shown explicitly in each bubble integrand.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12980e0b-66d1-430b-8e25-b7fe85c8742f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tadpole", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"eba0e395-0f0b-484c-8101-6316609f0b0b"],

Cell["\<\
Close the two graviton legs of the contact vertex with one graviton \
propagator. The massless gravitational tadpole is scaleless in dimensional \
regularisation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d8bc0a6-57d5-4de9-92a4-7f333a390c0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FermionPolarizationOperator1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
         "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "k", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
          RowBox[{"-", "k"}]}], "}"}], ",", "p", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "k"}], 
       "]"}]}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000100219991323*^9, 4.000100226292326*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"72dc86ab-5bc1-45dc-9bb2-5fcb848d135f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bubble", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4100daf2-e76e-4b48-9948-87f84ad93719"],

Cell["\<\
Join two three-point vertices with a graviton and a matter propagator. Dirac \
products use Dot; do not replace them by ordinary multiplication. \
GravitonFermionVertex takes graviton triples {index, index, incoming \
momentum}; include these momenta even when older examples list only the \
indices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c30d6f1-09a4-4648-9006-97853b969d7b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FermionPolarizationOperator2", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", 
            RowBox[{"-", "k"}]}], "}"}], ",", "p", ",", 
          RowBox[{"-", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
        RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}], ".", 
        RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "k"}], "}"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "k"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000100017951889*^9, 4.000100045710164*^9}, {
  4.0001002233223257`*^9, 4.000100274973031*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1df3d17e-21ea-4d67-8223-4ef140f2d76b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Combined operator", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"48e9a845-0c47-445d-afb0-a3fa703b557d"],

Cell["\<\
Add the stored tadpole and bubble terms and collect their scalar master \
integrals.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95394321-ab58-4e63-b2d5-8fbb6ea2a694"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FermionPolarizationOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"FermionPolarizationOperator1", "[", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", "m"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"FermionPolarizationOperator2", "[", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"C0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000100063016651*^9, 4.0001000799837837`*^9}, 
   4.000100132825869*^9, 4.000100210467094*^9, {4.000100286552602*^9, 
   4.000100290717547*^9}, 4.000100327372871*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1e4a7441-f817-48bd-86a8-8ebefbef1834"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Display and compare the result", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000100355124539*^9, 
  4.000100355390025*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8033b331-8a9a-4381-ae3c-\
a887d251b9dc"],

Cell["Apply Explicit before Dirac simplification. The displayed four-dimensional coefficients still contain unevaluated scalar loop integrals; setting D to four does not perform ultraviolet subtraction.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ae17b34-fecd-45d3-b5c1-b170bcf5bb74"],

Cell["Display the coefficients of the identity and slash p, then check that they reconstruct the computed expression. This tests the decomposition, not an independent reference formula.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57d75d85-8b5b-4005-8595-b3f6d59f5bad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fermionFourDimensional", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"DiracSimplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
         RowBox[{"FermionPolarizationOperator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", "m"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"DiracOrder", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}], "/.", 
      "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
      RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}], ",", "_DiracGamma", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", "#1", "]"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}],
   ";", 
  RowBox[{"fermionSlash", "=", 
   RowBox[{"FCI", "[", 
    RowBox[{"GS", "[", "p", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"fermionIdentityCoefficient", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Factor", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
     RowBox[{"fermionFourDimensional", ",", "fermionSlash", ",", "0"}], "]"}],
     "]"}]}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"fermionSlashCoefficient", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Factor", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
     RowBox[{"fermionFourDimensional", ",", "fermionSlash", ",", "1"}], "]"}],
     "]"}]}], ";", 
  TagBox[GridBox[{
     {"\"\<Identity\>\"", "fermionIdentityCoefficient"},
     {"\"\<Slash p\>\"", "fermionSlashCoefficient"}
    },
    AutoDelete->False,
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
    GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
    GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
   "Grid"]}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000100142994049*^9, 4.000100175815559*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f01d58b9-9b9e-4f66-ba51-aaddff3643f5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"fermionReconstructionCheck", "=", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"DiracSimplify", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
       RowBox[{"fermionFourDimensional", "-", "fermionIdentityCoefficient", "-", 
        RowBox[{"fermionSlashCoefficient", " ", "fermionSlash"}]}], "]"}], 
      "]"}], ",", "_DiracGamma", ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", "#1", "]"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], "\[Equal]",
    "0"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6d59492d-bbbf-4659-b0fa-0cef2258ca3c"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Massive vector", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0b4e23d8-57a6-4fc4-be9e-0b465693581d"],

Cell["\<\
The external matter legs are amputated. The internal graviton and matter \
propagators are shown explicitly in each bubble integrand.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5732ee4f-2771-49cc-b19d-a659a677618f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tadpole", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"3c73fa5a-ba2d-4644-a9e6-0314903368e3"],

Cell["\<\
Close the two graviton legs of the contact vertex with one graviton \
propagator. The massless gravitational tadpole is scaleless in dimensional \
regularisation.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3ba30ca-ad86-4252-b75e-c5e682842d74"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ProcaPolarizationOperator1", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonMassiveVectorVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "\[Rho]", ",", "\[Sigma]"}],
          "}"}], ",", "\[Mu]", ",", "p", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "\[Rho]", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", "k"}],
        "]"}]}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2755e4f7-11b5-41dd-b446-d545f21e3ee8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bubble", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f5448d39-5234-416c-8046-d76e7c2a8f67"],

Cell["\<\
Join two three-point vertices with a graviton and a matter propagator. Dirac \
products use Dot; do not replace them by ordinary multiplication. \
GravitonFermionVertex takes graviton triples {index, index, incoming \
momentum}; include these momenta even when older examples list only the \
indices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab7c2b7f-31cd-4f39-8b9d-35bbccc576be"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ProcaPolarizationOperator2", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "p_", ",", "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonMassiveVectorVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], ",", "\[Mu]", ",", "p", 
        ",", "\[Lambda]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonMassiveVectorVertex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Rho]", ",", "\[Sigma]"}], "}"}], ",", "\[Tau]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "\[Nu]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"-", "p"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "\[Rho]", ",", "\[Sigma]", ",", "k"}],
        "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"ProcaPropagator", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", ",", "\[Tau]", ",", 
        RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5c6b4432-acf4-41cf-b2f5-46f69f770012"]
